      "claim": "Tylocrebrine, a related phenanthroindolizidine alkaloid, showed rapid brain accumulation with an AUCbrain of 2.1 µg·h/mL in mice, directly demonstrating CNS access for this alkaloid class.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C12"],
      "claim": "Isocorydine, an aporphine alkaloid, effectively crossed the BBB in rats, with considerable brain levels detected within 10 minutes of administration.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C02"],
      "claim": "Corynoline, a tetracyclic isoquinoline alkaloid sharing methylenedioxy and tertiary-amine features with the query, traversed the BBB in mice and achieved relatively high brain concentrations.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "Hernandezine reached brain concentrations nearly equal to plasma Cmax after IV administration in rats, confirming meaningful CNS exposure for a complex alkaloid.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C01"],
      "claim": "A structurally related PET tracer with methoxyphenyl and piperidine motifs exhibited excellent brain penetration in rhesus monkey (SUV 5.6), supporting CNS access for this chemotype.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C10"],
      "claim": "Schisandrol B, a polycyclic natural product with similar lipophilicity, was detected in rat brain after oral administration, supporting BBB penetration.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is noscapine, a phthalideisoquinoline alkaloid with favorable passive BBB properties (logD 2.87, TPSA 75.7, HBD 0, neutral fraction 0.97). Multiple high-transfer experimental analogues—especially corynoline, isocorydine, tylocrebrine, and hernandezine—directly demonstrate brain penetration for closely related alkaloid scaffolds. The only negative analogue is a permanently charged quaternary ammonium with negligible transfer relevance. Therefore, meaningful CNS access is predicted.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct brain tumor/glioma pharmacokinetic data for the query itself; evidence is from related alkaloids in normal or peripheral tumor models.",
    "The only negative analogue (magnoflorine) is a permanently charged quaternary ammonium with very low transfer score and is not applicable to the neutral query."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
